From 639a66ee28aaa77579faaad2794f78356e05ffd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toly <1397674+AnatolyRugalev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 19:50:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom: an <img> shows the source srcset, sizes and
 <picture> choose

Blitz loaded an <img>'s src and nothing else: a srcset was ignored, and
an image given only by srcset, or by the <source> elements of a
<picture>, was never loaded.

BaseDocument::image_source now selects an image source as HTML does:
the first <source> of the <img>'s <picture> whose `type` this build
decodes (image's reading formats, and SVG) and whose `media` matches the
device, else the <img>'s own srcset, else its src. Of a srcset, the
candidate with the smallest density at or above the device's
(hidpi_scale times zoom), else the densest; a `w` candidate's density is
its width over the size `sizes` gives it (stylo's SourceSizeList), and
an <img>'s src counts as its 1x candidate when no other is. `media` is a
stylo MediaList, evaluated against the stylist's device.

load_image fetches that source, and changing an <img>'s srcset or sizes,
or a <source>'s srcset, sizes, media or type, loads the <img> again. Not
done: choosing again when the viewport or scale changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
